00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:48,000
A life lived in fear... is a life half lived.

2
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:30,000
Strictly Ballroom is a comedy, drama, romance film directed by Baz Luhrmann.

3
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:12,000
Brave new steps put Scott's career in jeopardy.

4
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:54,000
With a new partner and determination, can he still succeed?

5
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:36,000
Scott Hastings, played by Paul Mercurio.

6
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:18,000
Fran, played by Tara Morice.

7
00:32:54,000 --> 00:33:00,000
Barry Fife, played by Bill Hunter.

8
00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:42,000
Shirley Hastings, played by Pat Thomson.

9
00:42:18,000 --> 00:42:24,000
Liz Holt, played by Gia Carides.

10
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:06,000
Les Kendall, played by Peter Whitford.

11
00:51:42,000 --> 00:51:48,000
Strictly Ballroom is a 1992 Australian romantic comedy film directed and
co-written by Baz Luhrmann in his feature directorial debut.

12
00:56:24,000 --> 00:56:30,000
The film is the first in his Red Curtain Trilogy of theatre-motif-related films;
it was followed by 1996's Romeo + Juliet and 2001's Moulin Rouge!

13
01:01:06,000 --> 01:01:12,000
Strictly Ballroom is based on a critically acclaimed stage play, originally set up in 1984 by Luhrmann and
fellow students during his studies at the National Institute of Dramatic Arts in Sydney.

14
01:05:48,000 --> 01:05:54,000
An expanded version of the play became a success at the
Czechoslovakian Youth Drama Festival in Bratislava in 1986.

15
01:10:30,000 --> 01:10:36,000
In 1988, it had a successful season at Sydney's Wharf Theatre, where it was seen
by Australian music executive Ted Albert and his wife Antoinette.

16
01:15:12,000 --> 01:15:18,000
They both loved it, and, when Albert, soon after, set up the film production company M&A Productions with ex-Film
Australia producer Tristram Miall, they offered Luhrmann their plan to transform his play into a film.

17
01:19:54,000 --> 01:20:00,000
He agreed on the condition that he would also get to direct it.

18
01:24:36,000 --> 01:24:42,000
The film explores themes of dance, husband wife relationship,
dancer, parent child relationship, transformation.

19
01:29:18,000 --> 01:29:24,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
